WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.922
This module is about more than display formatting.

00:00:02.922 --> 00:00:06.037
A trailing space can create a different category.

00:00:06.037 --> 00:00:09.057
Inconsistent case can fragment groups.

00:00:09.057 --> 00:00:13.697
A date stored as text cannot safely participate in date arithmetic.

00:00:13.697 --> 00:00:16.467
Time values also have different meanings.

00:00:16.467 --> 00:00:23.512
A calendar date is different from a local clock timestamp, and both are different from an instant stored

00:00:23.512 --> 00:00:28.272
with time-zone meaning. The goal is to prepare these values without accidentally changing what they mean.

00:00:28.272 --> 00:00:33.047
Keep a real project in mind as we work through this section—for example,

00:00:33.047 --> 00:00:36.692
a hospital calculating length of stay and follow-up dates.

00:00:36.692 --> 00:00:43.272
The technical feature matters because it changes what questions we can answer reliably and how easily another

00:00:43.272 --> 00:00:44.952
analyst can understand our work.

00:00:44.952 --> 00:00:51.437
As you listen, try to connect each SQL or data concept to a decision you might need to

00:00:51.437 --> 00:00:55.957
defend later: what the data means, what one row represents, what can be missing,

00:00:55.957 --> 00:00:58.711
and what assumptions the transformation introduces.
